Z||000000||Ozzy||05-11-2000||12:38 AM||||O.K. So I figured it could be a hub assy. on my '88 Coupe. I have noticed that when I corner to the right the noise stops. It stays when cornering to the left. I was thinking that the right hand cornering was de-loading the rear pass. side wheel causing the noise to stop. I purchased a rear hub assy. today and installed it tonight and the damn problem is still there. I suspected that it was not the problem after removing the old assy. It feels just fine. Nothing rubbing in the transaxle at the spindle side either.<P>I guess I will pull apart the drivers side tommorow night and check it out. Maybe it's the short drive axle. I can get a replacement from the local Napa store for $47.00. I can't believe they had one sitting on the shelf. It maybe the bearing but wouldn't the cornering scenario described above point to the pass. side??<P>Ozzy||||reg||8
Z||000001||1FST2M6||05-11-2000||09:38 AM||||I had a similar noise.. was the front of the car. Drivers side wheel bearing.. but the resonance in the car made it sound like the rear of the car... Also had another annoying noise VERY much like the first.. ended up being the front brake caliper rattling replaced it and POOF no noise.. never had braking problems just weird resonance in the car. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ozzy||05-11-2000||11:29 AM||||Hmmmm...This noise sounds almost as if the wheel lining were rubbing on the tire tread. The sound is constant but varies in pitch with vehicle speed.<P>I am going to look into it some more tonight. It is beginning to piss me off!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ozzy||05-12-2000||12:23 AM||||Update for those interested! <P>Found it...it was the drivers side rear hub assy. Pulled it out and it felt rough. Placed another one in and ... viola! No more bloody noise! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||10
